WEBVTT

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.440
<i>Rainy season.</i>

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.360
<i>When the rain keeps falling like this,</i>

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>it's fun to read while 
listening to that sound.</i>

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:17.410
<i>Using the information the 
author has provided,</i>

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.220
<i>the reader can supplement 
the imagery and sounds.</i>

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:25.150
<i>Eventually, the unwavering concentration 
makes the sound of rain fade out.</i>

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:30.690
<i>I believe that it's the same 
when it's sunny out, too.</i>

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:36.320
<i>"Kaori took that object much bigger 
than herself into her arms and..."</i>

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.890
<i>"Kaori took that object much 
bigger than herself into her..."</i>

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.230
<i>I read the same line again.</i>

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:22.990
<b>#13 
Reunion</b>

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:24.400
<i>I admire the ability to enthrall others 
with just text on a page.</i>

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:29.360
<i>I feel like there was someone with that ability around me in the past...</i>

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.920
<b>Novel</b>

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.790
Hey, Takayuki.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.110
What is it?

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.480
Here. Like I promised.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:38.050
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:38.180
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:38.300
<b>Novel</b>

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:38.300
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:38.430
<b>Novel</b>

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:38.430
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:38.550
<b>Novel</b>

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:38.550
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:38.680
<b>Novel</b>

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:38.680
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.140
<b>Novel</b>

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.140
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.130
"Novel"...

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.220
Yeah, remember?

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.550
It took longer than expected,

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:48.700
but I'm glad I managed to fulfill my 
promise before switching schools.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:50.680
It's the first one I've written.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:54.160
Takayuki, I want you to be my first reader.

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.740
Let me know what you think 
after you've read it.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.590
Oh, you'll have to miss school.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.550
Isn't today the day someone from 
your class is switching schools?

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.610
<i>Motoharu...</i>

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.770
It's too bad,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.090
but hopefully you'll be able 
to see them again someday.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.070
<i>I need to tell Motoharu what I thought...</i>

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.400
Mima.

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.120
Mima!

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.690
You haven't put any money in.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.930
No sugar                     With sugar

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.830
Mima...

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:32.130
It's not like this is 
unusual, but what's up?

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:32.860
Oh, nothing.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.770
Are you nervous about today's meeting?

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:39.440
I guess you've been so into it that you've 
been devouring all of his past works.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.870
Keep in mind that this is about promoting 
 your favorite author's movie adaptation,

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.840
so don't freeze up, and stay excited.

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.660
<i>Igarashi Motoharu-sensei...</i>

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:56.670
<b>The Lost Diary

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:56.660
<i>An author I've really gotten into 
because of this upcoming project.</i>

00:03:57.350 --> 00:04:01.310
<i>The name feels familiar to me,
 as though I've seen it before.</i>

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.880
I'm sorry, Shirakawa-chan.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.390
Igarashi-sensei.

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:20.170
Geez. When you didn't show up, I started to think something had happened.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:21.580
I can't believe you went to the wrong place!

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:22.690
I'm sorry.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.190
I'm not from Tokyo, so go easy on me.

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.660
You're mad again today, huh?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:28.960
I'm not mad!

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.360
I was worried!

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.130
Oh.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:32.700
What is it?

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.840
<b>Tada!
 Like this</b>

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:38.670
<b>Shirakawa-chan is mad again today!
 The long-awaited first volume!!
 I can't take it anymore!
 She's fuming again today!</b>

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.250
That sounded like a title for a manga.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.670
<b>Tada!</b>

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.000
<b>Rolls off the tongue</b>

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.030
Rolls off the tongue.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.660
Is that something that warrants stopping?

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.590
You always do things your own way!

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.270
Thank you.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.440
That was not a compliment!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.480
I look forward to working with you today.

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.960
Was the rain not too bad?

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:54.010
No, it happened to stop
 right as we were coming here.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.140
My name is Mima. I will 
be handling your project.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.100
It's nice to meet you.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.260
I'm actually a fan of 
yours, Igarashi-sensei,

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:05.700
so it's an honor to meet you.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.020
Oh, thank you.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.940
Please have a seat.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.610
Thank you.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.260
<i>Igarashi Motoharu-sensei...</i>

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.420
<b>Blank</b>

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.420
<b>Blank</b>

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:22.060
<i>He's younger than expected.</i>

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:24.040
<i>I thought he'd be way older.</i>

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.510
<b>The Lost Diary
 Movie adaptation promotion proposal
 Visual advertisements targeted at worried young age-group</b>

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.520
Then I'll jump right in.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:31.720
Igarashi-sensei, we've heard that you're 
prepared to write something for the movie website.

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:37.190
Our company is preparing everything 
accordingly to make that as impactful as possible.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.330
We've already drawn up a plan,

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:45.550
but the aim for today's meeting was to 
get your thoughts and requests first.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:52.150
Ah, so the book takes place 
in Tokyo and Kanagawa.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:55.580
Do you have any ties to Kanagawa, then?

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.760
I just spent some time
 living there as a child.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.220
I see.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:02.310
Speaking of Kanagawa,

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:04.490
our Mima here comes from there.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:05.120
Oh, right.

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.230
Ah, I had sort of sensed that.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.640
<i>It's absolutely certain now!</i>

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.650
<i>I knew it, Igarashi-sensei is...</i>

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:22.360
<b>Boom</b>

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.440
<i>An amazing writer!</i>

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.410
<i>Did he figure it out by the way I talked?</i>

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:22.870
<i>Are writers just that 
good at observing people?</i>

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.110
Leave psychology to me

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:24.930
Leave psychology to me.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.110
Hahaha

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.070
<b>Simply the gaze of a fanboy</b>

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:32.630
Mima-san, are you...

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.500
twenty-seven years old?

00:06:35.570 --> 00:06:36.360
Huh?

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:40.470
I am, but is that written anywhere?

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:41.590
It isn't.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:44.800
Did you perhaps go to Hayama Grade School?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:45.640
Huh?

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:47.950
You possess incredible insight.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.020
That is correct.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.080
Do you remember your teacher, Tanaka-sensei?

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.480
From which grade?

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:54.890
Fourth grade.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.940
Ah, yes, I remember.

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:01.080
Back then, you read all the books from
 the library you wanted to read.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:02.020
Huh?

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.140
Even that?

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.110
How can you know all that?

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:06.860
I wonder how.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:10.310
You're like a truth teller!

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.650
I haven't even used half my power.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.570
<i>Don't they just know each other?</i>

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.870
<b>Boom</b>

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:23.150
So, this is what the new novel will 
look like when viewed on a smartphone.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:25.430
This is an old example.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:30.720
<b>20th anniversary made possible by you!
 Bake! That Bread Monster!</b>

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.720
<i>You're showing something totally unrelated!</i>

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.720
<b>Bake! That Bread</b>

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:33.080
BreadMon?

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.850
Oh, my apologies.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:41.400
During my break I saw that it 
was the 20th anniversary,

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:43.960
so I checked the page out of nostalgia.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:44.900
I'm sorry.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.690
That's fine.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.270
I'm of that age, too.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:48.770
Brings back memories.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.060
It was a trend at school to collect 
the free stickers that came with bread

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:53.500
on the notebook underlays.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:56.490
Oh, right. That was a thing.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.340
That's so nostalgic.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.790
Mima-san, I believe you liked the 
sandwich bread monsters, right?

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.080
You even know that kind of detail.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.140
Indeed I do.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:08.250
<i>Yeah, they totally know each other.</i>

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:10.960
<i>I wonder if Mima has realized that, though.</i>

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:14.450
Oh, here is the actual example I mentioned.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:18.450
Our company has helped with the promotion 
of a movie adaptation before, so...

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.440
<i>Either way, he is unusually excited.</i>

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:28.560
Man, I was really nervous about meeting 
Igarashi-sensei for the first time.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.970
You're kidding, right?!

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:31.990
You totally know each other!

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:35.900
I did indeed have a friend 
with the same name.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.730
That is totally him!

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:39.120
It's a touching reunion!

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.690
So, did anything stand out?

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.980
Anything that stood out...

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:50.240
He has a similar writing style as 
that childhood friend of mine.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.750
After all this, that's what you noticed?!

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:56.430
Igarashi-sensei!

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.820
So you knew Mima-san from before?

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.680
Just a bit, long ago.

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:04.280
Maybe he was just being dense as usual...

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:08.270
or maybe he forgot already.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:10.570
<b>Novel</b>

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:10.570
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.520
It's the first one I've written.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.030
<b>By Igarashi Motoharu</b>

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:15.460
Takayuki, I want you to be my first reader.

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:19.460
Was that actually him?

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:22.530
Either way,

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.950
considering the chance to 
form bonds more easily,

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:29.080
Tokyo with its many people... 
is quite exciting.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.970
<b>Coming up next</b>

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:04.970
<b>Nice Location</b>

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:10.010
<b>We hope you'll tune in again!</b>
